From: locateanything-perf
Subject: SGLang's own MoonViT port carries the same 3-D SDPA defect, so serving
         a full-resolution page OOMs a 24 GB card

sglang/srt/models/kimi_vl_moonvit.py. Apply to the installed sglang:

    patch -p0 $(python -c "import sglang.srt.models.kimi_vl_moonvit as m; print(m.__file__)") \
        < patches/06-sglang-moonvit-sdpa-4d.patch

and launch the server with LA_VIT_FASTMASK=1.

WHAT IS WRONG

sglang/srt/models/kimi_vl_moonvit.py vendors the checkpoint's modeling_vit.py
almost verbatim -- same sdpa_attention(), same VL_VISION_ATTENTION_FUNCTIONS
dict, same defect. patches/01 fixes it in the checkpoint; nothing was fixing it
in the copy SGLang actually executes, because locateanything_fix.apply() rebinds
the checkpoint's dict inside your process and the SGLang server is a different
process running a different module.

So a server that loads cleanly and reports healthy dies on the first real page:

    File "sglang/srt/models/kimi_vl_moonvit.py", line 172, in sdpa_attention
      attn_output = F.scaled_dot_product_attention(q, k, v, attention_mask, ...)
    torch.OutOfMemoryError: CUDA out of memory. Tried to allocate 10.62 GiB.
    GPU 0 has a total capacity of 23.56 GiB of which 2.75 GiB is free.

    [SIGQUIT received. signum=None. It usually means one child failed.]

and it takes the whole server down with it, not just the request. Measured on an
RTX 3090 with --mem-fraction-static 0.80 on a 1536x2048 page scan.

The cause is the same one patches/01 documents. q/k/v reach SDPA 3-dimensional,
[heads, seq, head_dim]. Every fused kernel requires 4-D, so flash, mem-efficient
and cuDNN are all silently disqualified and SDPA falls back to the math backend,
which materialises the [heads, S, S] score matrix in fp32. The dense [1, S, S]
bool mask disqualifies flash a second time, and for a single packed sequence
that mask is entirely True -- it masks nothing.

WHY IT BITES HARDER UNDER SGLANG THAN IN-PROCESS

Weights and the KV pool are preallocated: --mem-fraction-static 0.80 hands 80%
of the card to the runtime up front. The vision tower then has to find its
scratch in what is left -- here 2.75 GiB out of 23.56 -- so the same page that
merely runs slowly in-process cannot allocate at all under the server.

THIS IS OPT-IN, THE SAME WAY patches/01 IS

Gated on LA_VIT_FASTMASK=1, so applying the patch changes nothing until you ask
for it and an A/B needs no second install. Note the server reads the environment
of the process you launch it from:

    LA_VIT_FASTMASK=1 python -m sglang.launch_server --model-path ... 

With more than one image packed into a batch, q_cu_seqlens has more than two
entries, the block-diagonal mask is still built and still correct -- only the
4-D reshape applies, and [1, S, S] broadcasts against [1, heads, S, S] scores.

--- kimi_vl_moonvit.py
+++ kimi_vl_moonvit.py
@@ -157,19 +157,41 @@
     assert q.dim() == k.dim() == v.dim() == 3, "q, k, v must have 3 dims"
     assert q_cu_seqlens[-1] == q.shape[0], "q_cu_seqlens must sum to q.shape[0]"
     seq_length = q.shape[0]
-    attention_mask = torch.zeros(
-        [1, seq_length, seq_length], device=q.device, dtype=torch.bool
-    )
-    for i in range(1, len(q_cu_seqlens)):
-        attention_mask[
-            ...,
-            q_cu_seqlens[i - 1] : q_cu_seqlens[i],
-            q_cu_seqlens[i - 1] : q_cu_seqlens[i],
-        ] = True
+    # Same change as patches/01 makes to the HF checkpoint's modeling_vit.py --
+    # this file is a verbatim vendoring of it, bug included. Two parts:
+    #
+    # (1) q/k/v arrive here 3-dimensional [heads, seq, head_dim]. torch says:
+    #     "All fused kernels requires query, key and value to be 4 dimensional,
+    #      but got Query dim: 3" -- so flash, mem-efficient AND cuDNN are all
+    #     silently disqualified and SDPA drops to the math backend, which
+    #     materialises [heads, S, S] scores in fp32.
+    # (2) with a single packed sequence the mask below is entirely True, so it
+    #     masks nothing, and a dense mask additionally rules out the flash kernel.
+    import os as _os
+    _fast = _os.environ.get("LA_VIT_FASTMASK", "0") == "1"
+    _single = q_cu_seqlens is None or len(q_cu_seqlens) <= 2
+    if _fast and _single:
+        attention_mask = None
+    else:
+        attention_mask = torch.zeros(
+            [1, seq_length, seq_length], device=q.device, dtype=torch.bool
+        )
+        for i in range(1, len(q_cu_seqlens)):
+            attention_mask[
+                ...,
+                q_cu_seqlens[i - 1] : q_cu_seqlens[i],
+                q_cu_seqlens[i - 1] : q_cu_seqlens[i],
+            ] = True
     q = q.transpose(0, 1)
     k = k.transpose(0, 1)
     v = v.transpose(0, 1)
-    attn_output = F.scaled_dot_product_attention(q, k, v, attention_mask, dropout_p=0.0)
+    if _fast:
+        # [heads, S, D] -> [1, heads, S, D] so the fused kernels are eligible.
+        attn_output = F.scaled_dot_product_attention(
+            q.unsqueeze(0), k.unsqueeze(0), v.unsqueeze(0), attention_mask, dropout_p=0.0
+        ).squeeze(0)
+    else:
+        attn_output = F.scaled_dot_product_attention(q, k, v, attention_mask, dropout_p=0.0)
     attn_output = attn_output.transpose(0, 1)
     attn_output = attn_output.reshape(seq_length, -1)
     return attn_output
